        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 30",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 30,
          "component_id": "6b7c107f-79d6-5ca8-9f4b-28d56c5935d9",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3101,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:30",
          "start": 3012
        },
        "quote": "(h) Color and Finish. The generator and tower shall be a nonreflective and neutral color.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:30#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 31",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 31,
          "component_id": "313e43c9-9a54-5081-b1d7-2c1267152831",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3280,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:31",
          "start": 3102
        },
        "quote": "(i) Decibel levels for the system shall not exceed 55 decibels (dBA) measured at any property line, except during short-term events such as utility outages and severe windstorms.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:31#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 32",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 32,
          "component_id": "8df3730f-c186-584e-9c00-8a59f2b1d38d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3452,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:32",
          "start": 3281
        },
        "quote": "(j) Compliance with All Applicable Codes. A wind energy system including tower shall comply with all applicable building and property codes currently in force in the City.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:32#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 33",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 33,
          "component_id": "e7eebca6-0703-5199-8b62-a16f8c2dbe1e",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3901,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:33",
          "start": 3453
        },
        "quote": "(k) Utility Notification and Interconnection. All wind energy systems that connect to the facilities of an electrical utility company shall comply with all applicable local, State and Federal regulations governing such connections. The applicant or property owner must supply the Development Services Division with written consent from the applicable electric utility company to connect to the grid at the time of application for a building permit.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:33#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 34",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 34,
          "component_id": "2e9cdabd-4aeb-578c-b228-b357e55a04c2",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3914,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:34",
          "start": 3902
        },
        "quote": "(l) Signage.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:34#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 35",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 35,
          "component_id": "e1ac26a0-d144-5fd1-88cf-df29ceb96a1e",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3990,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:35",
          "start": 3915
        },
        "quote": "(1) Brand names shall not be visible from any public right-of-way or place.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:35#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 36",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 36,
          "component_id": "209a86d0-d43b-5be7-8ee1-c5bd48fdecda",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4057,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:36",
          "start": 3991
        },
        "quote": "(2) No advertising shall be placed on the wind generator or tower.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:36#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 37",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 37,
          "component_id": "afef5f8b-b5c4-5633-8c2b-5165c9cfc089",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4173,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:37",
          "start": 4058
        },
        "quote": "(m) Wind generators or towers shall not be artificially lighted, except as may be required by Federal or State law.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:37#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 18.265.030 block 38",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 38,
          "component_id": "415b644a-85bb-51cd-bbd3-167c813dc816",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 4967,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:38",
          "start": 4174
        },
        "quote": "(n) Removal of Abandoned Wind Energy Systems. Any wind energy system that is not operated for a period of 12 continuous months or which was operated under a conditional use permit which has expired and has not been renewed shall be considered abandoned, and the owner of such wind energy system shall remove the same within 90 days of a receipt of notice from the Planning Director notifying the owner of such required removal. If such wind energy system is not removed within said 90 days, the City Council may cause the removal of such wind energy system at the owner’s expense. If there are two or more users of a wind energy system, then this provision shall not become effective until all users have ceased using the system for a period of 12 continuous months. (Ord. 19598 § 3, 6-28-11.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.265.030:block:38#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
